{"schema_version":1,"source_commit":"100560de6c9f68c2875097d40a2012a84c784179","scope":"Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam Canto 2, Chapter 8 — Śrīdhara Svāmī word-for-word gloss","source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","entries":[{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":1,"end":2,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["अष्टमे","in the eighth [canto]"],["देह-सम्बन्धम् आक्षिपन्","questioning the relationship with the body"],["ईश-जीवयोः","between the Lord and the living being"],["बहून् परीक्षित् आपृच्छत्","Parīkṣit asked many questions"],["पुराण-अर्थान् बुभुत्सितान्","wishing to know the meanings of the Purāṇa"],["ब्रह्मणेति त्रिभिः","with three verses beginning ‘to Brahmā’"],["अगुणस्य गुणातीतस्य अपि","of the quality-less one, although beyond the qualities"],["देववत् दर्शनं यस्य सः","one whose appearance is like that of a god"]],"note":"The source groups 2.8.1–2 in one Śrīdhara block; the WFW range preserves it."},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":3,"end":3,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["निःसङ्गं मनः","the mind free from attachment"],["श्री-कृष्णे निवेश्य","having fixed it on Śrī Kṛṣṇa"],["स्व-प्रयत्नः दर्शितः","one's own effort is shown"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":4,"end":4,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["श्रद्धया शृण्वतः","of one who hears with faith"],["न आवश्यकः","not necessary"],["स्व-प्रयत्नं विना","without personal effort"],["भगवान् स्वयम् एव","Bhagavān himself alone"],["हृदि विशति","enters the heart"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":5,"end":5,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["भाव-सरोरुहं हृदय-कमलम्","the heart-lotus, the lotus of emotion"],["प्रविष्टः","having entered"],["तद्-गतं सर्वं मलम्","all the impurity residing there"],["धुनोति","he removes"],["द्रव्यान्तर-व्यामिश्रणादिना","by mixing with another substance and the like"],["कुम्भ-स्थे जले शोधिते","when water in a pot is purified"],["नदी-तडागादि-गतम् न","not that which is in a river or lake"],["सावशेषम्","with something remaining"],["सर्वेषां सर्वं पापं निःशेषं हरति","he removes all the sin of everyone completely"]],"note":"The source joins “भाव-सरोरुहंहृदय”; the WFW separates the heart-lotus phrase and records the typographic defect."},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":6,"end":6,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["कृतार्थः भवति","he becomes fulfilled"],["धौतात्मा निष्पापः","with a cleansed self, sinless"],["राग-द्वेष-आदयः सर्वे परिक्लेशाः मुक्ताः","all afflictions, such as attachment and aversion, are released"],["पान्थः प्रवासाद् आगतः","a traveler who has returned from a journey"],["स्वस्य शरणं गृहं यथा न मुञ्चति","just as he does not leave his home, his refuge"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":7,"end":7,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["श्रवण-औत्सुक्यम्","eagerness to hear"],["सन्दिग्धान् अर्थान्","uncertain matters"],["अधातुमतः धातवः महा-भूतानि","the elements are the great elements"],["तत्-सम्बन्ध-शून्यस्य","of one without a connection to them"],["लौकिकस्य आत्मनः जीवस्य","the ordinary self, the living being"],["धातुभिर् देह-आरम्भः","the body begins from the elements"],["यदृच्छया निर्निमित्तम्","arising without cause, by chance"],["कर्म-आदिना हेतुना वा","or with action and the rest as cause"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["ईश्वरः","the Lord"],["एतत्-तुल्य-देहवान् प्रोक्तः","is also said to have a body like this"],["लोकानां संस्थानं रचना","the arrangement, the formation of the worlds"],["त्रैलोक्य-आत्मकं पद्मम्","the lotus consisting of the three worlds"],["यस्य उदरात् आसीत्","which arose from his belly"],["इयत्ता-युक्तैः स्व-परिमितैर् अवयवैः","with limited, measured limbs"],["यावान् यत्-सङ्ख्याक-अवयव-युक्तः","as large and with as many limbs"],["संस्थावान् अवयवान् इव प्रोक्तः","said to possess form and limbs"],["को विशेषः तस्य","what is his distinction?"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["अवश्यं विशेषः वाच्यः","a distinction must indeed be stated"],["अजः ब्रह्मा","the unborn Brahmā"],["भूतानां व्यष्टि-उपाधीनाम् आत्मा नियन्ता","the inner self and controller of beings' individual adjuncts"],["समष्टि-उपाधित्वात्","because he is the collective adjunct"],["येन अनुगृह्णता","by whom, when he was favored"],["तस्य रूपं ददृशे दृष्टवान्","he saw his form"],["ईक्षया अभिचोदितः","impelled by a glance"]],"note":"The source joins “तस्यापि द्रष्टुः”; it is separated in the WFW as “तस्य अपि द्रष्टुः”."},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["प्रश्न-अन्तरम्","another question"],["यत्र शेते","where he lies"],["येन रूपेण अवतिष्ठते","in the form in which he remains"],["विश्वस्य स्थिति-आदयः","the maintenance and the other conditions of the universe"],["यस्मात्","from whom"],["सर्व-अन्ते क्रियया सम्बन्धः","the action connects with the end of the sentence"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["पुरुषस्य अवयवैः","by the limbs of the Person"],["पूर्वं कल्पिताः","conceived previously"],["यस्य इह अवयवैः लोकान् कल्पयन्ति","by whose limbs the worlds are formed"],["लोकैः च अमुष्य अवयवाः","and the worlds are his limbs"],["पातालम् एतस्य पाद-मूलम्","Pātāla is the root of his foot"],["त्वन्-मुखात् श्रुतवन्तः वयम्","we heard it from your mouth"]],"note":"The source joins “एतस्यहि”; the WFW separates it as “एतस्य हि” and records the spacing repair."},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["सन्देह-विपर्ययाभ्याम् पृष्टम्","having asked through doubt and contrary views"],["अज्ञातान् बहून् अर्थान्","many unknown matters"],["कल्पः महान्","kalpa is a great period"],["विकल्पः अवान्तरः","a vikalpa is a smaller period"],["भूतादिः शब्दः यस्मात्","from which the word bhūtādi comes"],["सतः स्थूल-देह-अभिमानिनः","of embodied beings identifying with the gross body"],["आयुषः प्रमाणम्","the measure of lifespan"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":13,"end":13,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["अनुमान-प्रकारः पृष्टः","having asked about the method of inference"],["विशेषं पृच्छति","he asks for a particular detail"],["कालस्य अनुगतिः प्रवृत्तिः","the course of time is its activity"],["कर्म-गतयः कर्म-प्राप्याणि स्थानानि","the destinations attained through action"],["यादृशीः","of what kinds"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":14,"end":14,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["गुणानां सत्त्व-आदीनाम् परिणामः","the transformations of the qualities, beginning with sattva"],["देव-आदि-रूपम् इच्छताम् गुणिनाम्","of those embodied beings desiring the forms of gods and the rest"],["यस्मिन् परिणामे","in which transformation"],["कर्मणां पुण्य-पापानां समुदायः","the aggregate of pious and sinful actions"],["केन कर्म-समुदायेन","by what collection of actions"],["कथं कृतेन","performed in what manner"],["कः अधिकारी","who is qualified"],["देव-आदि-भावं प्राप्नोति","attains the status of a god and the rest"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":15,"end":15,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["भू-पाताल-आदीनां सम्भवः","the arising of the earth, Pātāla and the rest"],["एतानि ओकांसि येषाम्","of those beings whose abodes these are"],["प्राणिनाम् सम्भवः","the origin of living beings"],["यथा इति सर्वत्र अनुषङ्गः","the phrase ‘how’ applies throughout"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":16,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["वर्णानाम् आश्रमाणां च","of the classes and stages of life"],["विनिश्चयः","determination"],["तत्-तत्-स्वभावैः","by their respective natures"],["निर्धारः","ascertainment"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["युगे युगे प्रतियुगम्","in every age"],["यः धर्मः","what dharma is"],["यच् च हरेः अवतार-अनुचरितम्","and the accounts of Hari's incarnations"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["स-विशेषः वर्णाश्रम-निबन्धनः","particular, governed by varṇa and āśrama"],["श्रेणीनाम्","of guilds"],["तत्-तद्-व्यवसाय-उपजीविनाम्","of those who live by their respective occupations"],["व्यवहार-नियम-लक्षणः धर्मः","dharma characterized by rules of conduct"],["राजर्षीणाम्","of royal sages"],["प्रजा-पालन-अधिकारिणाम्","those entitled to protect the subjects"],["कृच्छ्रेषु आपत्सु जीवताम् सर्वेषाम्","of all living beings during hardships and calamities"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":19,"end":19,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["सर्वेषां तत्त्वानां","of all principles"],["प्रकृत्य्-आदीनाम्","beginning with primordial nature"],["परिसङ्ख्यानं सङ्ख्या","enumeration means counting"],["लक्षणं स्वरूपम्","a characteristic is the essential nature"],["हेतुतः लक्षणम्","a characteristic by cause"],["तत्-तत्-कार्य-हेतुत्वेन","as the cause of the corresponding effects"],["पुरुष-आराधनस्य विधिः","the procedure for worshiping the Person"],["देव-पूजा-प्रकारः","the method of worshiping the deities"],["अष्टाङ्ग-योगस्य च विधिः","and the procedure for eight-limbed yoga"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":20,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["योगेश्वराणाम् ऐश्वर्येण","through the powers of yogīs"],["अणिमादिना","beginning with aṇimā"],["अर्चिरादि-गतिः","the path beginning with light"],["लिङ्ग-शरीरस्य भङ्गः प्रलयः","the dissolution of the subtle body"],["वेदा ऋग्-वेद-आदयः","the Vedas, beginning with the Ṛg Veda"],["उपवेदा आयुर्-वेद-आदयः","the auxiliary Vedas, such as Āyurveda"],["धर्माः धर्म-शास्त्राणि","the dharmas are the law books"],["इतिहास-पुराणयोः गतिः स्वरूपम्","the scope and nature of the epics and Purāṇas"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["सम्प्लवः अवान्तर-प्रलयः","a partial dissolution"],["सम्यक् प्लवनम् उद्भवः","complete rising means emergence"],["विक्रमः स्थितिः","vikrama means maintenance"],["प्रतिसंक्रमः महा-प्रलयः","return means the great dissolution"],["इष्टं वैदिकं कर्म","iṣṭa is Vedic ritual"],["पूर्तं स्मार्तम्","pūrta is a Smārta work"],["वापी-कूप-तडाग-आदि","stepwells, wells, tanks and the like"],["अन्न-प्रदानम् आरामः","giving food and gardens"],["त्रि-वर्गस्य धर्म-अर्थ-कामस्य विधिः","the procedure for duty, wealth and desire"],["अविरोध-प्रकारः","the manner that avoids conflict"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["अनुशायिनाम्","of those who remain after dissolution"],["लीन-उपाधीनाम्","whose adjuncts have dissolved"],["जीवानाम्","of the living beings"],["आत्मनः जीवस्य","of the individual self"],["व्यवस्थानम्","the settled state"],["बन्ध-मोक्ष-अतिरिक्त-स्वरूपेण अवस्थानम्","existing in a nature other than bondage or liberation"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["उदास्ते","he remains withdrawn"],["प्रलये","at dissolution"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["च-शब्दात्","from the word ‘and’"],["अपृष्टम् अपि","even what was not asked"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["प्रमाणं सम्यक् ज्ञाता","a reliable authority, one who knows correctly"],["ब्रह्म-नारद-व्यास-क्रमेण","through the succession of Brahmā, Nārada and Vyāsa"],["सम्प्रदायः अस्ति","there is a tradition"],["सामान्य-न्यायेन","by a general principle"],["त्वद्-अन्ये","those other than you"],["प्रायशः गतानुगतिकाः","mostly follow one another"],["न तत्त्व-विदः","they are not knowers of the truth"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["अशन-द्विज-कोपाभ्याम्","by fasting and the anger of brāhmaṇas"],["व्याकुलस्य","of one who is distressed"],["श्रवणम्","hearing"],["न परायन्ति न अपगच्छन्ति","they do not turn away, they do not depart"],["न व्याकुलीभवन्ति","they do not become disturbed"],["अच्युत-कीर्ति-पीयूषम्","the nectar of Acyuta's fame"]],"note":"The source spells “श्रवनम्” here; the WFW uses the conventional spelling “श्रवणम्” and records the source form."},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["उपामन्त्रितः पृष्टः","invited, questioned"],["संश् च असौ पतिः च","he who is a sage and a lord"],["तस्य","of him"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["ब्रह्म-कल्पे","in Brahmā's kalpa"],["सृष्टि-उपक्रम-कल्पे","the period at the beginning of creation"],["भागवत-आख्यानेन एव","through the Bhāgavata narration itself"],["प्रश्नानाम् उत्तरम्","the answers to the questions"],["दातुम् उपक्रान्तवान्","he began to give"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":8,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/08_parIxit-prashnaH.md","source_blob_sha":"b1545a87855e3040c49c9052aa7183073a2576e0","pairs":[["पाण्डूनाम् ऋषभः श्रेष्ठः","the foremost among the Pāṇḍavas"],["आनुपूर्व्येण","in sequence"],["प्रस्ताव-क्रमः","the order of presentation"],["न प्रश्न-क्रमः","not the order of the questions"]]}]}